{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29618 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Scalarolide is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular pathways involving the CD70 antigen. The evidence suggests that Scalarolide targets the CD70 antigen, which in turn is recognized by a complex of proteins, including the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, each linking Scalarolide to the CD70 antigen and ultimately to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The presence of multiple distinct molecular structures that are targets of Scalarolide, all of which are involved in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicates a broad and multifaceted mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of CD70 as a critical mediator in the interaction between Scalarolide and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Scalarolide modulates epigenetic processes through the regulation of this complex.",
